    if incompatible) alongside the hash re-bake, and bump stan4bart's
    Depends/LinkingTo dbarts floor in the same lockstep release - the
    load handshake covers the library-ahead direction, the floor covers
    consumer-ahead; both must move together.
  email tmle's maintainer (Susan Gruber) before the CRAN submission (VD
    2026-09-29): tmle's default learner libraries call dbarts::bart with
    BayesTree's argument names (tmle.SL.dbarts2, tmle.SL.dbarts.k.5:
    x.train, ntree, ndpost, ...), which 1.0-0 forwards to bartBT with a
    once-per-session warning and 1.1-0 stops forwarding, so tmle's
    defaults break then unless they call bartBT (version-guarded while
    they support 0.9-x). Also: the wrappers pass obsWeights
    unconditionally and pnorm() the latents; unit weights are handled
    dbarts-side, but genuinely weighted binomial analyses lose the dbarts
    learners by design, and family routing on their side would need the
    matching inverse link.
  at the freeze, dispatch stan4bart's sanitizers.yaml by hand against
    the final dbarts.h (VD 2026-09-26, dec-A36). At the merge, stan4bart's
    and treatSens's sanitizers.yaml move their dbarts ref from bartcore to
    main, and treatSens's branch filters to its default branch.
  at submission, re-run the FULL battery on the tip: R CMD check
    --as-cran on a clean-copy tarball, the suite, the equivalence
    trio against the current baselines (details in
    docs/plans/archive/cran-readiness.md), and the full 26-scenario
    comparison against 0.9-34 (benchmarks/R/classic-compare.R, VD
